 block applies (60 G block + 5 G fee)\");\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 105 G for 4 runes -- no block (4×25 G + 5 G fee)\");\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 180 G for 7 runes (7×25 G + 5 G fee)\");\n\n  // --- \"Alike\" components ---\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 80 G for 2 runes + 1 moonstone -- no block, different types (3×25 G + 5 G fee)\");\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 125 G for 3 runes + 3 moonstones -- two separate blocks (60+60 G + 5 G fee)\");\n\n  // --- Cursed modifier ---\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 155 G for a cursed sword (100 G + 50 G curse + 5 G fee)\");\n\n  // --- Highly enchanted modifier (enchantment >= 5) ---\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 140 G for a sword with enchantment 5 (100 G + 30 G enchantment + 5 G fee)\");\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 105 G for a sword with enchantment 4 -- no enchantment surcharge (100 G + 5 G fee)\");\n\n  // --- Cursed + highly enchanted combined ---\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 185 G for a cursed sword with enchantment 5 (100 G + 50 G curse + 30 G enchantment + 5 G fee)\");\n\n  // --- Loyalty discount (>= 2 years with MHPCO) ---\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 89 G for a sword with loyalty discount, 2 years with MHPCO (100 G - 20 G loyalty + 5 G fee)\");\n\n  // --- First insurance surcharge (10%) ---\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 115 G for a sword as first insurance (100 G + 10 G first insurance + 5 G fee)\");\n\n  // --- Follow-up contract discount (15% on each contract after first) ---\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 94 G for a sword as second contract (100 G - 15 G follow-up discount + 5 G fee)\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\"should apply cursed surcharge only to the cursed item, not policy total -- cursed sword (100 G), plain amulet (60 G) → 210 G before first-insurance/fee, final 236 G\");\n\n  // --- Integration example: Newcomer with cursed sword ---\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 165 G for newcomer (0 years, no previous contract) with cursed sword (steel, enchantment 3)\");\n\n  // --- Integration example: Long-standing customer's second contract ---\n  it.todo(\"should return premium 160 G for 3-year customer, second quote, cursed sword (enchantment 7)\");\n\n  // --- Integration: First insurance still applies to new item even on follow-up contract ---\n  it.todo(\"should apply first insurance surcharge even to long-standing customer's new item\");\n\n  // --- Rounding in MHPCO's favor ---\n  it.todo(\"should round premium 197.5 G → 198 G (round up)\");\n\n  // ============================================================\n  // CLAIM tests -- ordered simple to complex\n  // ============================================================\n\n  // --- Edge cases ---\n  it.todo(\"should exit with non-zero status for claim with damage entry whose item is not in policy\");\n  it.todo(\"should exit with non-zero status for claim with unknown item type in damages\");\n  it.todo(\"should exit with non-zero status for claim with negative damage amount (-200)\");\n  it.todo(\"should exit with non-zero status for claim with more damage entries of a type than insured\");\n\n  // --- Simple reimbursement ---\n  it.todo(\"should pay 400 G for regular sword (steel, enchantment 3), damage 500 G (500 - 100 deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"should pay 100 G for rune (insurance value 250 G), damage 200 G (200 - 100 deductible)\");\n\n  // --- Deductible per damage event ---\n  it.todo(\"should pay 600 G for dragon attack damaging sword (500 G) and amulet (300 G) -- deductible per item: (500-100)+(300-100) = 600\");\n\n  // --- Enchantment threshold (>= 8) ---\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse at 50% for enchantment >= 8: steel sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → 400 G (500 - 100 deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"should pay 700 G for dragon-material sword enchantment 5, damage 800 G — only dragon clause applies (800 - 100)\");\n  it.todo(\"should pay 400 G for dragon-material sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 G — 50% rule wins (500 - 100)\");\n\n  // --- Dragon material ---\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material items (minus deductible)\");\n\n  // --- Cap exhaustion ---\n  it.todo(\"should cap insurance at 1600 G for sword + amulet policy (insurance sum 1600, cap 3200)\");\n  it.todo(\"should have cap 2000 G for cursed sword (based on unmodified insurance value 1000)\");\n  it.todo(\"should have insurance sum 1750 G for sword + 3 runes block (1000 + 3×250); block discount does not affect sum\");\n  it.todo(\"should exhaust cap correctly: two successive claims of 1500 G each — first=1400 G, second=600 G\");\n\n  // --- Rounding for payouts ---\n  it.todo(\"should round payout 350.5 G → 350 G (round down)\");\n\n  // ============================================================\n  // MULTI-STEP scenario tests\n  // ============================================================\n\n  it.todo(\"should process a multi-step scenario: quote then claim sequentially\");\n  it.todo(\"should process a scenario with two quotes and a claim on the first policy\");\n  it.todo(\"should process the full schema example: quote amulet then claim on it\");\n\n  // ============================================================\n  // Output format tests\n  // ============================================================\n\n  it.todo(\"should output results array matching steps array length and order\");\n  it.todo(\"should include premium for quote steps and payout+remainingCap for claim steps\");\n});"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949195209},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me also check the current cli.ts after the\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_591c4609e759402586220770","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-12-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/cli.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":193