r(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100, amulet: 60, staff: 80, potion: 40, rune: 25, moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: unknown): { results: QuoteResult[] } => {\n  const scenario = input as Scenario;\n  validateItems(scenario.steps);\n  \n  const results: QuoteResult[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      let total = 0;\n      \n      const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n      for (const item of items) {\n        if (item.type === \"rune\" || item.type === \"moonstone\") {\n          componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n        } else {\n          total += BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n        }\n      }\n      \n      for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n        const blocks = Math.floor(count / 3);\n        const remainder = count % 3;\n        total += blocks * 60 + remainder * 25;\n      }\n      \n      total += 5;\n      results.push({ premium: total });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};\n```\n\n**Component Count (processScenario only — the core business logic)**:\n\n| Element | Count | Mass |\n|---------|-------|------|\n| Constants (string/number literals) | 12: `\"quote\"`×2, `\"rune\"`, `\"moonstone\"`, `0`×5, `3`×2, `60`, `25`, `5` | 12 |\n| Bindings (vars/params) | 8: `input`, `scenario`, `results`, `step`, `items`, `total`, `componentCounts`, `item` (inner) | 8 |\n| Invocations | 6: `validateItems()`, `as Scenario`, `step.items ??`, `item.type ===`, `componentCounts[item.type] ??`, `Object.values()`, `Math.floor()`, `results.push()` | 16 |\n| Conditionals | 3: `step.op === \"quote\"`, `if (rune/moonstone)`, `??` coalescing | 12 |\n| Loops | 3: `for (step of steps)`, `for (item of items)`, `for (count of Object.values)` | 15 |\n| Assignments | 3: `results.push`, `componentCounts[item.type] = …`, `total +=` (×3 counted once since same variable) — actually `total +=` appears 3 times, `componentCounts[...] =` 1 time, `results.push` 1 time | 30 |\n\nWait, let me be more precise:\n\nLet me recalculate more carefully:\n\n**Constants** (literals): `\"quote\"` (2), `\"rune\"` (1), `\"moonstone\"` (1), `0` (5 times: initial 0, `?? 0`, `?? 0` again, `% 3` — no `% 3` uses the number 3 not 0, `+ 0` not present), let me recount: `0` appears as initializer (`let total = 0`), in `?? 0` (once per component type assignment), in `?? 0` isn't quite right — `(componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1` has a `0`. So: `0` (total init), `0` (coalesce), `1` (increment). Plus `3` (appears twice: `/ 3`, `% 3`), `60`, `25`, `5`.\n\nConstants: `\"quote\"`×2, `\"rune\"`, `\"moonstone\"`, `0`×2, `1`, `3`×2, `60`, `25`, `5` = 13 × 1 = **13**\n\nBindings: `input`, `scenario`, `results`, `step`, `items`, `total`, `componentCounts`, `item` (loop1), `item` (loop2 — different scope reusing same name), `count` = 9 × 1 = **9**\n\nInvocations: `validateItems()`, `Object.values()`, `Math.floor()`, `results.push()`, `scenario.steps`, `step.items`, `count / 3`, `count % 3`, `blocks * 60`, `remainder * 25`, `total +=` (is assignment, not invocation) = hmm, operators are not invocations per se.\n\nLet me be strict about APP: invocations are function/method calls. `+`, `==`, `*` are operators and not counted as invocations.\n\nTrue invocations: `validateItems()`, `Object.values()`, `Math.floor()`, `.push()`, `??` (the operator itself, not a function). Actually coalescing `??` is an operator too.\n\nSo real invocations: `validateItems(scenario.steps)` = 1, `Object.values(componentCounts)` = 1, `Math.floor(count / 3)` = 1, `results.push({ premium: total })` = 1. Total: 4 × 2 = **8**\n\nBut `step.items` (property access) isn't an invocation. `scenario.steps` also not.\n\nConditionals: `if (step.op === \"quote\")` = 1, `if (item.type === \"rune\" || item.type === \"moonstone\")` = 1, the `||` inside it is part of the conditional. `??` operator is a conditional. Actually `??` is a binary operator, not a conditional statement. Let me count `if` statements and ternary `?:` only.\n\nConditionals: `if (step.op === \"quote\")` = 1, `if (item.type === \"rune\" || item.type === \"moonstone\")` = 1 = 2 × 4 = **8**\n\nLoops:\n- `for (const step of scenario.steps)` = 1\n- `for (const item of items)` = 1  \n- `for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts))` = 1\n= 3 × 5 = **15**\n\nAssignments:\n- `total = 0` = 1\n- `componentCounts[item.type] = ...` = 1\n- `total += blocks * 60 + remainder * 25` = 1\n- `total += 5` = 1\n- `results.push({ premium: total })` — push is an invocation, not an assignment\n= 4 × 6 = **24**\n\n**Total Mass**: 13 + 9 + 8 + 8 + 15 + 24 = **77**\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Apply Simple Design Rules\n\n### Rule 1: Tests Pass ✅ — All 8 tests pass\n\n### Rule 2: Reveals Intent\n\nIssues identified:\n1. **`componentCounts`**: The name is misleading — it counts \"component\" types but only rune and moonstone. A better name would be `componentTypeCounts` or just extract the logic.\n2. **Magic number `60` and `25`**: The block discount constants are inlined without explanation. The per-component base price (25) is used in 3 places (BASE_PREMIUMS, the 25 remainder multiplier, and the 60 block price which is effectively 2×25+10 or could be arbitrary).\n3. **The component logic mixing**: The base premium accumulation for non-components vs. components is split awkwardly — non-components get `total +=` in one loop, components get counted first then added in a separate loop.\n\n### Rule 3: No Duplication\n\n- `25` appears in BASE_PREMIUMS and in the remainder calculation — this is the same knowledge (individual component price). This is conceptual duplication.\n- `BASE_PREMIUMS` already contains the unit price for each type. The block discount logic re-derives 25 G by hardcoding, creating a knowledge gap.\n\n### Rule 4: Fewest Elements\n\n- The `?? 0` pattern is used, which is fine.\n- Could the two loops (one for non-components, one for component discounts) be merged? Possibly but that might reduce clarity.\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Implement Refactoring\n\nI'll focus on **Rule 2 (clarity)** and **Rule 3 (DRY)** by:\n\n1. Renaming `componentCounts` to `componentTypeCounts` for clarity\n2. Extracting the component discount logic into a helper function that uses `BASE_PREMIUMS` as the source of truth for per-unit price (no hardcoded `25` duplicate)\n3. Adding a named constant for the block size\n\nLet me compute the per-unit price from `BASE_PREMIUMS` and the block price by using the unit price:\n\nEach component (rune, moonstone) has `BASE_PER_PREMIUM = 25`. A block of 3 = 60. So the block discount is `3 * 25 → 60 → saving 15 per block`.\n\nLet me extract this clean"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c6a2f8d6f022461b96d5395c","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/cli.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: unknown): { results: QuoteResult[] } => {\n  const scenario = input as Scenario;\n  validateItems(scenario.steps);\n  \n  const results: QuoteResult[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      let total = 0;\n      \n      // Count component types for block discount\n      const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n      for (const item of items) {\n        if (item.type === \"rune\" || item.type === \"moonstone\") {\n          componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n        } else {\n          total += BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n        }\n      }\n      \n      // Apply block discount: every 3 alike components = 60 instead of 3×25\n      for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n        const blocks = Math.floor(count / 3);\n        const remainder = count % 3;\n        total += blocks * 60 + remainder * 25;\n      }\n      \n      // Processing fee\n      total += 5;\n      results.push({ premium: total });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};","newText":"const BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst calculateComponentTotal = (countsByType: Record<string, number>): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const count of Object.values(countsByType)) {\n    const blocks = Math.floor(count / BLOCK_SIZE);\n    const remainder = count % BLOCK_SIZE;\n    total += blocks * BLOCK_PRICE + remainder * 25;\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: unknown): { results: QuoteResult[] } => {\n  const scenario = input as Scenario;\n  validateItems(scenario.steps);\n  \n  const results: QuoteResult[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      let total = 0;\n      \n      const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n      for (const item of items) {\n        if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n        } else {\n          total += BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n        }\n      }\n      \n      total += calculateComponentTotal(componentCounts);\n      total += PROCESSING_FEE;\n      results.push({ premium: total });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":3511,"output":3386,"cacheRead":6144,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13041,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","times