     let total = 0;\n      \n      const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n      for (const item of items) {\n        if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n        } else {\n          total += BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n        }\n      }\n      \n      total += calculateComponentTotal(componentCounts);\n      total += PROCESSING_FEE;\n      results.push({ premium: total });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949305509},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\n\n## Step 5: Calculate New APP Mass\n\n**Core business logic** (`processStatement` + `calculateComponentTotal`):\n\n### `processScenario`:\n\n| Element | Count | Mass |\n|---------|-------|------|\n| Constants (literals) | `\"quote\"` (2), `\"quote\"` (1 actually since one `step.op === \"quote\"` and one conditional), `0` (2: total init, `?? 0`), `1` (increment) = 6 | **6** |\n| Bindings | `input`, `scenario`, `results`, `step`, `items`, `total`, `componentCounts`, `item` = 8 | **8** |\n| Invocations | `validateItems()`, `COMPONENT_TYPES.has()`, `calculateComponentTotal()`, `results.push()` = 4 | **8** |\n| Conditionals | `if (step.op === \"quote\")`, `if COMPONENTYPES.has(item.type)` = 2 | **8** |\n| Loops | `for (step of steps)`, `for (item of items)` = 2 | **10** |\n| Assignments | `total = 0`, `componentCounts[item.type] = . . . `, `total += calculateComponentTotal()`, `total += PROCESSING_FEE`, `results.push(.. . )` — wait push is invocation. Assignments: `total = 0`, `componentCounts[item.type] = ...`, `total += ... ` (2 times) = 4 | **24**\n\n`processScenario` subtotal: 6 + 8 + 8 + 8 + 10 + 24 = **64**\n\n### `calculateComponentTotal`:\n\n| Element | Count | Mass |\n|---------|-------|------|\n| Constants | `0` (init), `3` (BLOCK_SIZE is a binding, not a literal in this function — actually it's a reference to a const), `25` (hardcoded) = 2 | **2**