  85|   });\n     86|   it.todo(\"should return premium 180 G for 7 runes (7×25 G + 5 G fee)\"…\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[1/1]⎯\n\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  1 failed | 8 passed | 36 todo (45)\n   Start at  03:15:21\n   Duration  167ms (transform 30ms, setup 0ms, collect 29ms, tests 8ms, environment 0ms, prepare 44ms)\n\n ELIFECYCLE  Test failed. See above for more details.\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1784949322016},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Interesting - we get 90 not 105. That means the refactoring changed something. 4 runes = 1 block of 3 (60) + 1 remainder (25) = 85 + 5 fee = 90. But the spec says \"4 runes → 100 G base premium (no block — block requires exactly 3)\". \n\nThe spec says \"A building block of 3 alike components is offered at a special base premium of 60 G\" and \"4 runes → 100 G base premium (no block — block requires exactly 3)\". So the block only applies when there are EXACTLY 3 of a type — not for 3 among 4!\n\nLet me fix this. Red Phase Complete for test 9, now to Green.\n\nRed Phase Complete:\n**Test Activated**: \"should return premium 105 G for 4 runes -- no block (4×25 G + 5 G fee)\"\n**Compilation Prediction**: No compilation error Correct\n**Runtime Prediction**: expected 105, received 90 (block logic incorrectly applied for 4 runes — should be no block) Correct\n**Result**: Test fails — the block should only apply for exactly 3, not for groups of 3 in larger sets.\n\n## Green -- Fix block to \"exactly 3\" only\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e8f429ccf53d48aaa173cbd9","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-12-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/cli.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":2424,"output":369,"cacheRead":35072,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":37865,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949322018,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-fe08b741-017c-4424-bfd1-ba47031a0dc3","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e8f429ccf53d48aaa173cbd9","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"type QuoteResult = { premium: number };\n\ninterface QuoteItem {\n  type: string;\n}\n\ninterface Step {\n  op: string;\n  items?: QuoteItem[];\n}\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nconst VALID_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\"sword\", \"amulet\", \"staff\", \"potion\", \"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst validateItems = (steps: Step[]): void => {\n  for (const step of steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\" && step.items) {\n      for (const item of step.items) {\n        if (!VALID_ITEM_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst calculateComponentTotal = (countsByType: Record<string, number>): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const count of Object.values(countsByType)) {\n    const blocks = Math.floor(count / BLOCK_SIZE);\n    const remainder = count % BLOCK_SIZE;\n    total += blocks * BLOCK_PRICE + remainder * BASE_PREMIUMS.rune;\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: unknown): { results: QuoteResult[] } => {\n  const scenario = input as Scenario;\n  validateItems(scenario.steps);\n  \n  const results: QuoteResult[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      let total = 0;\n      \n      const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n      for (const item of items) {\n        if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n        } else {\n          total += BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n        }\n      }\n      \n      total += calculateComponentTotal(componentCounts);\n      total += PROCESSING_FEE;\n      results.push({ premium: total });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949325217},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I need to change the block logic: block only applies when the count is exactly 3 (or exactly 3 of the same type within a larger group). Wait, let me re-read the spec examples:\n\n- 2 runes → 50 G base (2×25 = 50, correct)\n- 3 runes → 60 G base (block applies)  \n- 4 runes → 100 G base (no block — block requires exactly 3)\n- 7 runes → 175 G base\n\nSo for 7 runes: 175 G. That's 7 × 25 = 175. No blocks at all because we have 7, not 3. So \"exactly 3\" means only when the total count per type is 3, not when we have 6 or 9 etc.\n\nActually wait: let me re-check. 7 runes = 175. That's exactly 7 × 25. No blocks at all even though 7 has a multiple of 3. So the block ONLY applies when ALL of that type are exactly 3. Interpreted strictly: only when count === 3.\n\nBut then what about \"3 runes + 3 moonstones → 120 G base premium (two separate blocks)\"? That's 60 + 60 = 120. Each component type has exactly 3, so block applies to each.\n\nSo the rule is: if the count of a component type is exactly 3, use the block price; otherwise charge individually"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1ff0219a7bcb4d1d8170c985","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"const calculateComponentTotal = (countsByType: Record<string, number>): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const count of Object.values(countsByType)) {\n    if (count === BLOCK_SIZE) {\n      total += BLOCK_PRICE;\n    } else {\n      total += count * BASE_PREMIUMS.rune;\n    }