premium 115 G for a sword as first insurance (100 G + 10 G first insurance + 5 G fee)\nAssertionError: expected { results: [ { premium: 105 } ] } to deeply equal { results: [ { premium: 115 } ] }\n\n- Expected\n+ Received\n\n  Object {\n    \"results\": Array [\n      Object {\n-       \"premium\": 115,\n+       \"premium\": 105,\n      },\n    ],\n  }\n\n ❯ src/cli.spec.ts:168:20\n    166|     };\n    167|     const result = processScenario(input);\n    168|     expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n       |                    ^\n    169|   });\n    170| \n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[2/3]⎯\n\n FAIL  src/cli.spec.ts > Claim Office CLI > should return premium 94 G for a sword as second contract (100 G - 15 G follow-up + 5 G fee)\nAssertionError: expected { premium: 105 } to deeply equal { premium: 115 }\n\n- Expected\n+ Received\n\n  Object {\n-   \"premium\": 115,\n+   \"premium\": 105,\n  }\n\n ❯ src/cli.spec.ts:178:31\n    176|     };\n    177|     const result = processScenario(input);\n    178|     expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n       |                               ^\n    179|     expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ premium: 94 });\n    180|   });\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[3/3]⎯\n\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  3 failed | 16 passed | 26 todo (45)\n   Start at  03:16:26\n   Duration  169ms (transform 32ms, setup 0ms, collect 31ms, tests 10ms, environment 0ms, prepare 42ms)\n\n ELIFECYCLE  Test failed. See above for more details.\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1784949386235},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three fail as expected:\n- Test 17: expected 89, got 105 (loyalty discount not applied)\n- Test 18: expected 115, got 105 (first insurance not applied)\n- Test 19: expected 115/94, got 105/105 (neither modifier applied)\n\nRed Phase Complete:\n**Test Activated**: Tests 17-19 (loyalty, first insurance, follow-up contract)\n**Compilation Prediction**: No compilation error Correct\n**Runtime Prediction**: All three expected to fail (policy-wide modifiers not implemented) Correct\n\n## Green -- Add policy-wide modifiers\n\nNow I need to add: loyalty discount (20% for ≥ 2 years), first insurance surcharge (10%), follow-up contract discount (15% each after first). These apply at the policy level.\n\nAlso need to track first insurance - every item is first insurance per the spec. So first insurance always applies to each item. But wait: the example says \"100 G base + 50 G curse + 10 G first insurance = 160 G + 5 G fee = 165 G\". That's 100 + 50(cursed) = 150, 150 + 10 (10% of 100) = 160. So first insurance is 10% of the base premium.\n\nBut actually, the items already have their base modified by cursed/enchantment. Policy-wide modifiers apply to the sum of all item base premiums.\n\nLet me implement: track policy-wide modifiers (loyalty, first insurance surcharge, follow-up discount) and apply them after item-level modifiers.\n\nFirst insurance: 10% on the total base premiums (sum of all items after item-level modifiers). Hmm wait, the spec says \"A first insurance carries a 10% initial assessment surcharge.\" and \"Customers receive a 15% discount on each contract after their first.\"\n\nThe spec example helps: \"Long-standing customer's second contract: 100 G base + 50 G curse + 30 G high enchantment − 20 G loyalty + 10 G first insurance − 15 G follow-up contract = 155 G + 5 G fee = 160 G\"\n\nSo order matters: item modifiers first (100, +50 curse, +30 enchantment = 180), then policy modifiers (-20 loyalty, +10 first insurance, -15 follow-up = -25), then: 180 - 25 = 155 + 5 = 160.\n\nWait: 100 + 50 + 30 = 180 base after items. Then -20% loyalty on 100 = -20. Then +10% first insurance on 100 = +10. Then -15% follow-up on 100 = -15. So: 180 - 20 + 10 - 15 = 155 + 5 = 160.\n\nSo loyalty, first insurance, and follow-up all act on the base premium of each item individually, just like cursed and enchantment. They're item-level modifiers! But they're described as \"policy-wide\". The distinction is: item-specific (cursed, enchantment) apply only to that item; policy-wide (loyalty, first insurance, follow-order) apply to all items.\n\nLet me re-read: \"item-specific modifiers (cursed, high enchantment) apply to the base premium of the affected item; policy-wide modifiers (loyalty, first insurance, follow-up contract) apply to the policy base premium (sum of all item base premiums)\"\n\nSo loyalty is 20% off the sum of base premiums. First is 10% on the sum. Follow-up is 15% off the sum.\n\nIn the integration example: 100 G base + 50 + 30 - 20 + 10 - 15 = 155. The subtraction of 20 (loyalty) is 20% of 100 (base of the single sword), and +10 is 10% of 100.\n\nSo for a single item they're the same, but for multi-item they'd be on the sum.\n\nThe spec says \"Long-standing customers (≥ 2 years) receive 20% loyalty discount\" on what? The integration example says on the policy base premium.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d9adee020d0f4e60b485ce6c","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"export const processScenario = (input: unknown): { results: QuoteResult[] } => {\n  const scenario = input as Scenario;\n  validateItems(scenario.steps);\n  \n  const results: QuoteResult[] = [];\n  let quoteIndex = 0;\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      let total = 0;\n      \n      const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n      for (const item of items) {\n        if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n        } else {\n          const base = BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n          let modifier = 0;\n          if (item.cursed) {\n            modifier += 0.5;\n          }\n          if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= 5) {\n            modifier += 0.3;\n          }\n          total += base * (1 + modifier);\n        }\n      }\n      \n      total += calculateComponentTotal(componentCounts);\n      \n      // Policy-wide modifiers\n      const baseTotal = total; // sum of all item premiums before policy modifiers\n      let policyModifier = 0;\n      if (scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2) {\n        policyModifier -= 0.2;\n      }\n      // First insurance surcharge: always applies (every item is first insurance)\n      policyModifier += 0.1;\n      // Follow-up discount: 15% on each contract after first\n      if (quoteIndex > 0) {\n        policyModifier -= 0.15;\n      }\n      \n      total = basePrice * (1 + policyModifier);\n      total += PROCESSING_FEE;\n      results.push({ premium: total });\n      quoteIndex++;\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};","oldText":"export const processScenario = (input: unknown): { results: QuoteResult[] } => {\n  const scenario = input as Scenario;\n  validateItems(scenario.steps);\n  \n  const results: QuoteResult[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      let total = 0;\n      \n      const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n      for (const item of items) {\n        if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n        } else {\n          const base = BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n          let modifier = 0;\n          if (item.cursed) {\n            modifier += 0.5;\n          }\n          if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= 5) {\n            modifier += 0.3;\n          }\n          total += base * (1 + modifier);\n        }\n      }\n      \n      total += calculateComponentTotal(componentCounts);\n      total += PROCESSING_FEE;\n      results.push({ premium: total });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-12-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/cli.ts"}