odifier applies to the sum of BASE premiums (before item modifiers). Not on the sum after item modifiers!\n\nLet me fix this: first insurance (10%) should apply to the raw BASE premiums, not the modified item premiums.\n\nFor the single cursed sword: base = 100. Item modifier: 100 + 50(curse) = 150. Policy modifier: 10% of 100 (base) = 10. Total: 150 + 10 + 5 = 165.\n\nRed Phase Complete:\n**Test Activation**: \"should return premium 165 G for newcomer with cursed sword\"\n**Compilation Prediction**: No compilation error Correct  \n**Runtime Prediction**: expected 165, received 170 (policy modifiers applied to total, should apply to base only) Correct\n\n## Green -- Fix policy modifiers to apply to base premiums"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0d0a3b5395ef47a5b310ca98","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-12-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/cli.ts","offset":67}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":667,"output":468,"cacheRead":81152,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":82287,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949455803,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ee50b34a-fe3c-4ea5-9645-686fe8af11a0","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0d0a3b5395ef47a5b310ca98","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      let total = 0;\n      \n      const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n      for (const item of items) {\n        if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n        } else {\n          const base = BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n          let modifier = 0;\n          if (item.cursed) {\n            modifier += 0.5;\n          }\n          if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= 5) {\n            modifier += 0.3;\n          }\n          total += base * (1 + modifier);\n        }\n      }\n      \n      total += calculateComponentTotal(componentCounts);\n      \n      // Policy-wide modifiers\n      const baseTotal = total; // sum of all item premiums before policy modifiers\n      let policyModifier = 0;\n      if (scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2) {\n        policyModifier -= 0.2;\n      }\n      // First insurance surcharge: always applies (every item is first insurance)\n      policyModifier += 0.1;\n      // Follow-up discount: 15% on each contract after first\n      if (quoteIndex > 0) {\n        policyModifier -= 0.15;\n      }\n      \n      total = baseTotal * (1 + policyModifier);\n      total += PROCESSING_FEE;\n      // Round in MHPCO's favor (round up for premiums)\n      total = Math.ceil(total - 0.0001);\n      results.push({ premium: total });\n      quoteIndex++;\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949458469},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I need to track the base sum separately from the\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0844f2f540ba40619c8b004a","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      let itemTotal = 0; // sum after item-level modifiers\n      let baseTotal = 0; // sum of raw base premiums for policy modifiers\n      \n      const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n      for (const item of items) {\n        if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n        } else {\n          const base = BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n          baseTotal += base;\n          let modifier = 0;\n          if (item.cursed) {\n            modifier += 0.5;\n          }\n          if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= 5) {\n            modifier += 0.3;\n          }\n          itemTotal += base * (1 + modifier);\n        }\n      }\n      \n      const componentTotal = calculateComponentTotal(componentCounts);\n      itemTotal += componentTotal;\n      \n      // Policy-wide modifiers apply to raw base premiums (non-component items + component base prices)\n      // For components, the base total is the per-unit cost counted\n      // But policy modifiers don't apply to component items per se - only to main items\n      // Actually, re-reading the spec: policy-wide modifiers apply to the \"policy base premium (sum of all item base premiums)\"\n      // The components are included in item base premiums\n      let policyBase = baseTotal;\n      for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n        policyBase += count * BASE_PREMIUMS.rune;\n      }\n      \n      let policyModifier = 0;\n      if (scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2) {\n        policyModifier -= 0.2;\n      }\n      // First insurance surcharge: always applies (every item is first insurance)\n      policyModifier += 0.1;\n      // Follow-up discount: 15% on each contract after first\n      if (quoteIndex > 0) {\n        policyModifier -= 0.15;\n      }\n      \n      let total = itemTotal + (policyBase * policyModifier);\n      total += PROCESSING_FEE;\n      // Round in MHPCO's favor (round up for premiums)\n      total = Math.ceil(total - 0.0001);","oldText":"      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      let total = 0;\n      \n      const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n      for (const item of items) {\n        if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n        } else {\n          const base = BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n          let modifier = 0;\n          if (item.cursed) {\n            modifier += 0.5;\n          }\n          if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= 5) {\n            modifier += 0.3;\n          }\n          total += base * (1 + modifier);\n        }\n      }\n      \n      total += calculateComponentTotal(componentCounts);